{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773080208,"nonce":"XeIQ5cgGwJTh/bFNncqwKXGO5xU=","title":"Auto-start: watcher picks up new issues automatically","message":"The watcher should poll the tracker for new issues and automatically start agent sessions for them.\n\n## Current behavior\nThe watcher only monitors existing sessions (Q\u0026A, reviews, orphans). Starting work on an issue requires manual `nightshift start \u003cid\u003e`.\n\n## Desired behavior\n1. Watcher polls tracker for new issues matching a filter (e.g., label `nightshift` or `auto-work`)\n2. For each new issue, runs `nightshift start \u003cid\u003e` automatically\n3. Tracks which issues it already started (to avoid duplicates)\n4. Configurable via WORKFLOW.md (polling interval, filter label, max concurrent sessions)\n\n## Result\nFully autonomous loop: new issue appears → agent picks it up → does the work → posts for review → reviewer comments `@nightshift revise` or `@nightshift accept`. No human intervention except the review step.\n\n## Implementation notes\n- Add `auto_start` section to WORKFLOW.md config (label filter, poll interval, max concurrent)\n- Watcher already has tracker access (lazy-initialized)\n- Need to track started issue IDs to avoid re-launching (file in .nightshift/ or in-memory set + session dir check)\n- Should respect max concurrent sessions to avoid resource exhaustion","files":null}]}